187
00:11:54.232 --> 00:12:00.824
Frequency beats recency under skew and scans, especially at small cache sizes, where every slot matters.

188
00:12:01.104 --> 00:12:06.885
W-TinyLFU's admission filter stops one-hit wonders from displacing hot keys.

189
00:12:07.165 --> 00:12:08.680
Frequency is history.

190
00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:12.480
When popularity shifts abruptly, frequency policies lag.

191
00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:19.928
This is why Caffeine adapts its window size and Redis decays LFU counters over time (lfu-decay-time).

192
00:12:20.208 --> 00:12:34.309
Sampled eviction (pick 5 random keys, evict the worst) is within 0.3 points of exact LRU and needs no linked list or per-access pointer updates, the reason Redis uses it (maxmemory-samples).

193
00:12:35.659 --> 00:12:48.374
Policy per workload: allkeys-lfu for catalogue-like data; volatile- when only TTL'd keys may be evicted; noeviction for anything you can't lose (sessions), with alerts well before the limit.

194
00:12:49.724 --> 00:12:51.879
Threading, protocol and pipelining.

195
00:12:52.159 --> 00:13:02.527
Redis: a single-threaded event loop executes commands (no locks, deterministic atomicity), with I or O threads (Redis 6 plus) for socket reads or writes.

196
00:13:02.807 --> 00:13:05.751
Memcached: multi-threaded with fine-grained locks.

197
00:13:06.031 --> 00:13:09.807
Dragonfly or KeyDB: shared-nothing multi-threading.

198
00:13:10.087 --> 00:13:13.756
The protocol (RESP) is simple text framing; parsing is cheap.

199
00:13:14.036 --> 00:13:15.423
Round trips dominate.

200
00:13:15.703 --> 00:13:24.492
L2's server did ~50k ops per second one command per round trip, and ~5 to 8x more with 16 commands pipelined.

201
00:13:24.772 --> 00:13:26.628
The same is true for real Redis.

202
00:13:26.908 --> 00:13:31.559
Batch with MGET, pipelines and Lua scripts (Ch 43 L3:

203
00:13:31.839 --> 00:13:36.532
800 round trips, then 30 ms, 2, then 0.6 ms).

204
00:13:37.882 --> 00:13:40.186
Locks matter only once round trips don't:

205
00:13:40.466 --> 00:13:43.346
L2's global lock showed only with pipelining.

206
00:13:43.626 --> 00:13:46.783
Slow commands block everyone in a single-threaded server:

207
00:13:47.063 --> 00:13:50.455
KEYS, huge SMEMBERS, big DELs, long Lua scripts.

208
00:13:50.735 --> 00:13:53.743
Disable or rename dangerous commands; use SCAN.

209
00:13:55.093 --> 00:13:56.779
